Chapter: FactStore

  cites Foreword chapter Hamt

  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

  cites Foreword chapter Sha256



 A FactKind is one of:

   DefinitionFact — a definition of a named entity.

   ProofFact — a proof artifact.

   VouchFact — an endorsement or attestation.

   PolicyFact — a policy declaration.

   CapabilityFact — a granted capability.



 A Fact is a record containing hash as the SHA-256 content identifier, kind as the classification, content as the raw body, author as the identity of the fact author, and timestamp as the creation time.



 A BareFactStore is a record containing facts, the content-addressed storage keyed by hash, and count, the number of stored facts.



 A StoreResult is a record containing store, the store state after the operation, and was-new, True when the fact was not already present.



 To fact-store-empty gives BareFactStore, an empty store with no facts.

 To fact-content-hash gives Text, the SHA-256 hex digest of the given content.

 To fact-create gives Fact, constructing a fact from a kind, content, author, and timestamp with a computed content hash.

 To fact-store gives BareFactStore, inserting a fact if no fact with the same hash exists; no-op on duplicate.

 To fact-load gives Maybe Fact, looking up a fact by its hash.

 To fact-has gives Boolean, True when a fact with the given hash exists.

 To fact-count gives Integer, the number of stored facts.

 To fact-is-replay gives Boolean, True when the hash already exists, indicating a duplicate.

 To fact-store-if-new gives StoreResult, inserting a fact and reporting whether the insertion was new.

 To fact-kind-name gives Text, the human-readable name of a FactKind.



 We say:



Section: Fact Types



  FactKind =

    | DefinitionFact

    | ProofFact

    | VouchFact

    | PolicyFact

    | CapabilityFact



  Fact = record {

    hash : Text,

    kind : FactKind,

    content : Text,

    author : Text,

    timestamp : Integer

  }



  BareFactStore = record {

    facts : HamtMap Fact,

    count : Integer between 0 and 4294967295

  }



Section: Store Operations



  fact-store-empty : BareFactStore = BareFactStore { facts = hamt-empty, count = 0 }



  fact-content-hash : Text -> Text

  fact-content-hash (content) = sha256-to-hex (sha256 (text-to-bytes content))



  fact-create : FactKind, Text, Text, Integer -> Fact

  fact-create (kind) (content) (author) (timestamp) =

    let hash = fact-content-hash content

    in Fact { hash = hash, kind = kind, content = content, author = author, timestamp = timestamp }



  fact-store : BareFactStore, Fact -> BareFactStore

  fact-store (store) (f) =

    if hamt-contains (store.facts) (f.hash) then store

    else BareFactStore { facts = hamt-set (store.facts) (f.hash) f, count = store.count + 1 }



  fact-load : BareFactStore, Text -> Maybe Fact

  fact-load (store) (hash) = hamt-get (store.facts) hash



  fact-has : BareFactStore, Text -> Boolean

  fact-has (store) (hash) = hamt-contains (store.facts) hash



  fact-count : BareFactStore -> Integer

  fact-count (store) = store.count



Section: Replay Deduplication



  fact-is-replay : BareFactStore, Text -> Boolean

  fact-is-replay (store) (hash) = hamt-contains (store.facts) hash



  fact-store-if-new : BareFactStore, Fact -> StoreResult

  fact-store-if-new (store) (f) =

    if hamt-contains (store.facts) (f.hash)

      then StoreResult { store = store, was-new = False }

    else StoreResult { store = fact-store store f, was-new = True }



  StoreResult = record {

    store : BareFactStore,

    was-new : Boolean

  }



Section: Fact Kind Helpers



  fact-kind-name : FactKind -> Text

  fact-kind-name (k) = when k

    is DefinitionFact -> "Definition"

    is ProofFact -> "Proof"

    is VouchFact -> "Vouch"

    is PolicyFact -> "Policy"

    is CapabilityFact -> "Capability"



